{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The iPad app and the Mac helper ship separately, so the identifiers and value formats they share live here in one Foundation-only module, and the helper links none of the HID code. HeadwireGATTContract owns the service and characteristic UUIDs, the source mode request the iPad publishes to ask the Mac for a video mode, and the pairing offer and answer that let the helper link pair over an encrypted Bluetooth link with no code. Each value starts with a version byte, and readers ignore bytes they do not know. It does not publish anything or talk to CoreBluetooth; HeadwireHID publishes the services, and the helper reads them."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The GATT identifiers and characteristic values the iPad publishes and the Mac helper reads.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/GATTContract"],"title":"Identifiers","anchor":"Identifiers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/SourceModeRequest","doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/SourceModeWireError"],"title":"Source mode","anchor":"Source-mode"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/PairingOffer","doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/PairingAnswer","doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/PairingOfferWireError"],"title":"Pairing","anchor":"Pairing"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"HeadwireGATTContract"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"HeadwireGATTContract","externalID":"HeadwireGATTContract","symbolKind":"module"},"schemaVers